<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="updated"><strong>Updated November 2026.</strong> This policy describes ArtCard.LA as it is today: a static, read-only archive. It replaces the October 18, 2011 policy written for the original LA-Artist.com site.</p>

<h2>What this site is</h2>
<p>ArtCard.LA is a public archive of ArtCards mailed in from 2009 to 2015. Submissions are closed. The site does not have user accounts, comments, payments, or sign-ups. It uses Google Analytics to understand how many people visit and which pages they view.</p>

<h2>What is published</h2>
<p>For each card in the archive, the site publishes the artist name, the ZIP-code neighborhood, and the artwork as submitted. That information was written on the cards when they were mailed in and was already published on LA-Artist.com. Artworks remain © their artists and are shared under a <a rel="license" href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/us/">Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 United States License</a>.</p>

<h2>Analytics</h2>
<p>This site uses Google Analytics 4, a web analytics service from Google. Google Analytics uses cookies and similar technologies to collect information such as the pages you view, how you reached the site, your approximate location, and your device and browser type. We use these reports only in aggregate, to see how the archive is used. Google processes this information under the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>; see also <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
<p>You can opt out of Google Analytics with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>, or by blocking or deleting cookies in your browser.</p>

<h2>What we do not collect</h2>
<p>This site does not ask visitors for personal information. It does not offer accounts, comment forms, payments, or mailing-list sign-ups, and it does not use advertising cookies.</p>
<p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which may log visitors’ IP addresses under GitHub’s own privacy policy.</p>

<h2>Asking for an update or removal</h2>
<p>To ask for an artwork or artist name to be updated or removed, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a> with the card’s artist name and ZIP code. You can also use the <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}">Contact</a> page.</p>

<h2>Links to other websites</h2>
<p>The site may contain links to other websites, including Instagram and MagCloud. Those sites have their own privacy practices. This policy does not cover them.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, we will post the updated text on this page.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>. See also the <a href="{{ '/terms-of-use/' | url }}">Terms of Use</a>.</p>
